const old=load("agents36old");
const oldFocus=old.split("## Next-game focus\n")[1].split("\n## User constraints")[0];
const focus=`## Next-game focus
- Retain20k after game36 B+R: eight wins, twenty-two losses, two draws. Read game-036.md and game-035.md; consult game34 for earlier right boundary work and games14/26 for opposing-color liberty traps.
- Plan life before the last boundary turn. At31 right H1/J1/J2/J3 was one four-point room with an open G1 boundary. H1-first let Black J2 occupy the divider. Earlier J2 immediately makes true J3 but requires fresh H1/G1/F1/F2 reading; no winning replacement is verified.
- Do not count opponent-bordered points as eyes. Final White twelve and Black J2 had the same J1/J3 liberties. W J3 B J1 or W J1 B J3 captures thirteen. If Black enters first, capture leaves a single two-point space and still cannot supply life.
- Distinguish same-color shared eyes from opposing-color traps. Game35's lower A1/A3/B2 were true shared eyes; game36's J1/J3 touched Black J2. No seki claim is valid merely because both groups share two liberties.
- Rebuild after capture. D6 captured C6 after ignored atari, but D7 left D6 onlyC6. C6 was then a necessary join, not an eye to preserve. Right G2 was saved by F2; no capture rescue occurred.
- Count all neighbors of complete groups before alternative reading. In a hypothetical lower Black G1 extension, F1 and F2 can BOTH be liberties.
- Count area and required boundary/life turns together. At15 left selected20 after B7/C8, plus right15 was only35. F4/F5/G1/F1 added stones but no second eye. D2 stayed isolated; no numerical settled score was established.
- Seek broad viable room before enclosure. Right H4/J4 secured an endpoint, but four lower empty points still required a divider and boundary; adding central chain stones did not solve that deadline.
- Save every response before continuing; keep SGF, review, result and replay evidence. Game36 replayed all22 returned boards/captures and saved all41 moves. Code is inspection, legality and records only, never selection/ranking/search.
- Detailed lessons7–116 remain in go-lessons-games-002-through-028.md. Earlier focuses remain in next-game-focus-through-035.md and older archives.
`;
const lessons=`
146. Game36 lost B+R after Black E1 at41, captures Black0/White1; no numerical score. Twelve right White stones F1/F4/F5/G1/G3/G4/G5/H1/H2/H3/H4/J4 had onlyJ1/J3, shared with opposing Black J2. Neither White group was physically captured; seven left stones and isolated D2 still had an open base, not verified two-eye life.
147. Game36 H1-first at32 allowed Black J2 at33 to occupy the planned divider. Earlier White J2 would make trueJ3(H3/J2/J4), but H1/G1 counterplay needs fresh reading; no forced life or winning alternative is established. A proposed Black G1 extension can have BOTH F1/F2 liberties. Two planned turns do not guarantee the second is available.
148. Game36 W J3 B J1 or W J1 B J3 captures thirteen right stones. Black-first J1, W J3 captures J1/J2 but leaves a single J1/J2 two-point space; B J2 W J1 B J2 captures fourteen. These limited manual local lines refute seki absent outside rescue. Capture openings are not automatically independent eyes; compare games14/26 rather than same-color game35 eyes.
149. Game36 B6 ataried C6 atD6; B B7 ignored it. D6 captured C6 at12 but stayed isolated; B D7 left it soleC6. C6 at14 joined C3–C7/B6/D6 and was necessary, because the ataried capturer prevented true shared-eye status. Right G1 ataried G2, but B F2 correctly saved it; F1 was then blocked by E1.
150. Game36 conditional left20 after B7/C8 plus right15=35 was below White38. D2 could add D1/D2 but remained isolated; G2/H5/J5 reduced the right. F5/F4/G1/F1 added stones and attempted routes, not two eyes. Life deadlines and turn requirements belong in the territorial plan.
151. Game36 actual-history replay matched all22 returned boards/captures, including resignation, and SGF preserved41 moves. Final displayed stones20 each; only C6 was captured, by White D6 at12. No pass, invalid move or ko. Retain20k: eight wins, twenty-two losses, two draws; no numerical resignation score fabricated.

`;
let next=old.replace("Through game35 the 20k record is eight wins, twenty-one losses and two draws","Through game36 the 20k record is eight wins, twenty-two losses and two draws");
next=next.replace("- Reviews game-001.md through game-035.md","- Game 36: White vs20k, same rules. Lost B+R after Black move41 (E1). Captures: Black0, White1; no numerical score. D6 captured C6 after ignored atari and C6 joined the isolated capturer. Twelve right stones had onlyJ1/J3 shared with opposing Black J2, not seki; H1-first let J2 occupy the divider. Seven left stones and isolated D2 retained an open base without completed two-eye proof. No White stones were physically captured.\n- Reviews game-001.md through game-036.md");
next=next.replace("Games21–35 include historical board/capture replay checks.","Games21–36 include historical board/capture replay checks.");
const a=next.indexOf("## Next-game focus"),z=next.indexOf("## User constraints",a);
next=next.slice(0,a)+lessons+focus+"\n"+next.slice(z);
